# The in-session surface: keys you press and commands you type at its prompt.
# None of it appears in `claude --help`, which is the whole reason KEYS and HELP
# are separate views — a single --help dump would show this half as empty.
# /help inside a session is always the authoritative list; this is the short one.
name:    claude
what:    Claude Code, from the inside. Routed through the gateway by common.sh
check:   claude
docs:    /help inside a session

= WHILE YOU ARE IN IT
Shift-Tab        | cycle permission mode: ask -> accept edits -> plan
Esc              | interrupt what it is doing, keep the session
Esc Esc          | go back and edit an earlier message
Ctrl-c           | cancel the current input
Ctrl-d           | leave the session
Ctrl-l           | clear the screen
Up               | your previous prompts

= TYPING SOMETHING OTHER THAN A PROMPT
/                | a command — /clear, /compact, /model, /config, /tasks
@                | a file or directory, completed as you type
!                | run a shell command without leaving the session
#                | remember this — appends to the project's CLAUDE.md
Ctrl-v           | paste an image from the clipboard

= SESSION HOUSEKEEPING
/help            | every command and key this build has. Start here
/clear           | throw away the context and start fresh in place
/compact         | summarise the conversation to win back room
/model           | switch model for this session
/tasks           | background tasks and watches this session owns
/config          | settings, including the permission mode default
/doctor          | check the installation
